Choose collection meaning before its representation (@computing-collections: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Trace-mutation-and-sharing-across-a-collection-boundary.lingua#r_0E243F4674D6A5A66298639599") { r_0DB3963B09301C36C2DB916930
A collection is more than a container holding values. Its meaning includes which distinctions an operation must preserve. Revisit [Give every input a meaning and a checkable schema](../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/data/Meaning-and-schema.lingua#r_6R0FJMACN4F6T6R0ETDCQHF6NH) and [Specify inputs, results and failure before implementing](Specify-inputs-results-and-failure-before-implementing.lingua#r_0F6547BECCF6CA21F43948497D) before choosing a representation. For a synthetic arrival log `[("b", 20), ("a", 10), ("b", 21)]`, the first field is a category key and the second is an integer payload. The key is not a unique event identity. A real observation log would need an explicit event identifier, units and provenance; these integers deliberately carry no physical claim.

A sequence distinguishes position: exchanging the first two arrivals changes the sequence. Repeated equal elements remain separate occurrences. A set answers membership while forgetting multiplicity and sequence order. A multiset retains the count of each value while forgetting its position. A key-to-value mapping associates each key with one value, which can itself be a collection. These abstract meanings do not dictate one programming language or memory layout.

For the key sequence `b, a, b`, the set of keys is `{a, b}` and the multiset has two occurrences of b and one of a. Neither reconstructs arrival order. Repeatedly assigning a single dictionary value under b replaces the earlier payload; a mapping from b to a sequence of payloads can preserve both. Decide which result the application promises before using an operation that forgets information. Python dictionaries preserve insertion order, but that does not make repeated assignments under one key a history of arrivals. Python sets do not promise sequence order. See the concrete contracts in [Python tutorial and standard-library references — Python documentation](../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/sources/Python-Reference.lingua#r_53J5SVX9CRECPQJFX3EAD8NRCZ).

A position is relative to a particular sequence: inserting an earlier item changes later positions. A stable identifier can remain attached to the same conceptual item through reordering. Our category key is stable through sorting but permits many occurrences, so it cannot identify one occurrence on its own. Equal keys, equal complete rows and identical in-memory objects are three different statements. A program may need to preserve occurrences even when complete rows compare equal.

An abstract interface specifies observations and permitted operations. Its representation is how the implementation stores enough information to honor them. The same duplicate-aware lookup contract could use an unsorted sequence, an ordered sequence or a mapping to groups. Choosing one also chooses maintenance and resource costs. MIT's [Introduction to Algorithms — MIT 6.006, Spring 2020](../sources/Introduction-to-Algorithms-MIT-6006.lingua#r_04AEC4B446A81994AEEB84801D) lecture 2 supplies the interface/representation distinction; its named Set interface uses unique keys and ordered operations. Do not equate that course interface with Python's built-in set or our duplicate-preserving catalog.

**Read and work:** revisit Sundnes chapter 3, especially lists, nested lists, slicing and tuples, then chapter 7's dictionary opening through [Introduction to Scientific Programming with Python — Sundnes](../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/sources/Scientific-Python-Sundnes.lingua#r_1V7KWH76GSD7XMA9TQVSTEQSWB). Construct the sequence, set, multiset counts and grouped mapping for five arrivals with a repeated identical row. State what each representation loses. Explain why a dictionary key must be hashable: being described loosely as immutable is insufficient, as a tuple containing a list illustrates. Hash-function design and implementation remain later work.

**Continue:** [Trace mutation and sharing across a collection boundary](Trace-mutation-and-sharing-across-a-collection-boundary.lingua#r_0E243F4674D6A5A66298639599).

**Return:** [Computing](../Computing.lingua#r_02FE84C805C79A9D396F478641).
